# {{ kb_title }}: agent guide

{{ kb_description }}

The knowledge base follows the LLM-wiki pattern. `kb/` is an **Open
Knowledge Format (OKF) v0.2 bundle**{% if obsidian %} and, at the same time, an **Obsidian vault**{% endif %}.
You compile sources into interlinked pages, and the human curates, reads and
asks questions. Every edit must keep `kb/` a conformant bundle.

## Map

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `kb/` | The bundle{% if obsidian %} and vault{% endif %}. Every `.md` here is a concept page or a reserved `index.md`/`log.md`. |
| `schema/vocabulary.yaml` | Page `type`s: meaning, allowed folders, body sections. Also the typed-relation keys. |
| `schema/taxonomy.yaml` | Folder tree with titles and descriptions; these feed the generated indexes. |
| `schema/frontmatter.schema.json` | Core frontmatter field shapes (template-managed; extend via `fields` in the vocabulary). |
| `.agents/skills/` | Workflows: `kb-ingest`, `kb-query`, `kb-maintain`. |
| `justfile`, `tools/kbtools/` | Commands (`just` lists them) and the `kb` CLI behind them. |
| `.cache/` | Gitignored scratch space: fetched source text, drafts. |

## Workflows

- **Ingest**: a URL or document to add, or "read/add/summarize this" → skill `kb-ingest`.
- **Query**: a question the knowledge base should answer → skill `kb-query`.
- **Maintain**: lint, health check, cleanup, reorganizing → skill `kb-maintain`.
- **Personal notes**: folders in the "Personal" and "Vault" groups of
  `schema/taxonomy.yaml` belong to the human. Edit them when asked. When you
  write on the human's behalf, `generated.by` is still you.

## OKF hard rules

These make `kb/` a bundle. Breaking any of them breaks conformance.

1. Every `.md` file in `kb/` other than `index.md` and `log.md` starts with
   YAML frontmatter that has a non-empty `type`. Anything else goes in
   `.cache/` or outside `kb/`.
2. `index.md` files are **generated**. Change titles, descriptions and
   `schema/taxonomy.yaml`, then run `just fix`.
3. `log.md` is newest-first under `## YYYY-MM-DD` headings. Add entries only
   with `uv run kb log <Op> "<text>"`.

## Page profile

```yaml
---
type: Concept                      # from schema/vocabulary.yaml
title: CAP theorem
description: One sentence that stands alone; it becomes the index entry.
aliases: [Brewer's theorem]        # optional, helps search
tags: [distributed-systems]        # kebab-case, cross-cutting only
status: stable                     # draft while incomplete; deprecated when superseded
generated: { by: <tool>/<model>, at: 2026-09-25T12:00:00Z }   # you, UTC, updated on every meaningful edit
sources:
  - id: brewer-2012                # stable key cited as [^brewer-2012]
    resource: /sources/brewer-2012.md
    title: CAP twelve years later
depends_on: ["[Consistency models](/systems/distributed/consistency-models.md)"]
---
```

- Create pages with `uv run kb new <Type> <folder/slug.md> --title … --description … --tags … --by <tool>/<model>`
{% if claude_code %}  (Claude Code sets `KB_ACTOR`).{% else %}  (or set `KB_ACTOR`).{% endif %} The skeleton gives you the type's sections.
- **Citations.** Every non-obvious claim carries a footnote `[^id]` matching
  a `sources[].id`. The footnote definition links the Source page:
  `[^id]: [Title](/sources/slug.md)`. What you add from your own knowledge
  must be unambiguous in the prose.
- **Trust.** Add `verified: { by: human:{{ owner_id }}, at: … }` only when the
  human says they reviewed that page. Never mark your own work verified.
- **Freshness.** Set `stale_after` on pages whose facts expire (versions,
  pricing, roadmaps).

## Links and relations

- Link other pages with standard markdown links using **bundle-absolute**
  targets: `[CAP theorem](/systems/distributed/cap-theorem.md)`. Wikilinks
  (`[[…]]`) are not part of OKF.
- A link to a page that doesn't exist yet is allowed: it marks a wanted page.
- **Typed relations** are frontmatter lists of markdown links, using the keys
  in `schema/vocabulary.yaml`. Each target must also be linked in the body,
  in prose that says why.

## Placement

- **One concept per page.** Search before creating (`just find`, `rg -il`,
  folder `index.md`), and extend an existing page rather than creating a
  near-duplicate.
- The folder follows the type (`vocabulary.yaml`) and the topic
  (`taxonomy.yaml`). Keep the tree at most 3 levels deep.
- Add a subfolder once about 5 pages share a subtopic. Register it in
  `schema/taxonomy.yaml` in the same change.
- File and folder names are kebab-case. Move or rename pages with
  `uv run kb mv <old> <new>`, which rewrites every inbound link and the indexes.

## Done

A change is done when:

- `just check` reports 0 errors (in Claude Code, hooks enforce this);
- knowledge edits have a `log.md` entry;
- you have told the human which pages changed.

Commit only when the human asks.
